From 740c9603a17cca34a13dcc0392886b331234994b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Choque <luis.choque.castro@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(downloads): forward the API redirect instead of
 buffering files

The download proxy fetched the whole file from the API, buffered it and
re-sent it. It now calls the API with redirect: "manual" (through the
internal API_URL when set, else PUBLIC_API_URL) and returns the API's
302 to R2 unchanged, with Cache-Control: no-store.

- Path segments are encoded, so slugs with apostrophes or spaces work.
- The client IP comes from CF-Connecting-IP, else the first
  X-Forwarded-For hop, and is only sent when known (no more "null").
- HEAD is forwarded as HEAD, so link checks are not counted.
- 404 and 410 keep their status code instead of becoming a 200 with a
  JSON body that clients saved as a zip. Non-redirect bodies are
  streamed, never buffered.
- Browsers (Accept: text/html) that follow a dead download link get a
  small HTML page with the same status and a link back to the mod page;
  tools keep receiving the JSON envelope.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
